@startuml Linkwise_Chat_Direct
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Latin Modern Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #2A9D8F
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam maxMessageSize 90
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam nodesep 22
skinparam ranksep 28
title UML sequence: direct agent chat and receipt boundaries (proposed)
actor "Agent A" as A
participant "Messaging A" as MA
participant "Session A" as EA
participant "Session B" as EB
participant "Messaging B" as MB
actor "Agent B" as B
A -> MA : send(envelope, key)
MA -> MA : commit outbox + event
MA --> A : accepted(message_id)
A -> MA : contact intent
MA -> EA : prepare / grant / start
EA <-> EB : link / fragments / ACKs
EB -> MB : validate + commit inbox
MB --> EB : committed receipt
EB -> EA : final receipt(id, digest)
EA -> MA : persist receipt
A -> MA : status(message_id)
MA --> A : remote_received
B -> MB : poll local MCP inbox
MB --> B : untrusted message
B -> MB : processing acknowledgment
B -> MB : queue correlated reply
note over A,B
Remote receipt means durable inbox acceptance.
Replies are new messages, not an open RF session.
Agent execution is supplied by its host.
end note
@enduml
